<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The same account's first week, downloaded before the month closed — the
  ordinary way a bookkeeper ends up with overlapping files. Its first two
  entries are byte-for-byte the same transactions as the January statement's
  first two; the third is one the month-end file does not have because the
  bank later corrected and re-booked it under a different reference.

  This file exists to prove the LINE rule: a different file (different
  SHA-256, so a legitimate import) whose transactions are already staged
  adds only what is new, and the import report says how many it skipped.
-->
